the intended destination.
11. Open the loop at one link and observe that the ring's data flow is interrupted.
Mesh topology
12. Using the available patch cords, connect each node module directly to every other
node module.
13. Transmit between two nodes and observe that, because multiple direct paths exist,
communication continues even if one link is removed — demonstrating fault
tolerance.
14. For each topology, record on the observation sheet: number of cables used, the path
taken by the data, and the effect of a single link or node failure.

RESULT:
Thus, the bus, star, ring and mesh network topologies were studied and physically
constructed on the Benchmark LAN Trainer Kit.
